#
# Fold-Safe Conservative Weak Supervision
#
# PURPOSE
# -------
# Answer one controlled question as quickly as possible:
#
#   Does fold-safe report-derived weak supervision improve the
#   reproduced W3.0/V4 gold-only MRI baseline?
#
# W3.1 changes ONLY the supervision channel.
#
# Kept from W3.0:
#   - cached frozen ImageNet ResNet18 slice features
#   - exact V4/W2.3 5-fold split
#   - same trainable projection / slice attention / series fusion
#   - zero-metadata V4 ablation
#   - same series attention / classifier
#   - 12 fixed epochs
#   - AdamW lr=1e-3, wd=1e-4
#   - CosineAnnealingLR eta_min=1e-6
#   - gold BCE pos_weight = neg/pos clipped [1,5]
#   - batch size 1
#   - no early stopping
#
# Added:
#   - ONE fold-specific W2.3 pseudo study per gold optimizer step
#   - only W2.3 SoftLabelAvailable cells
#   - only CandidateSelectionScore >= 0.50 cells
#   - continuous SOFT probability targets, never hard 0/1
#   - sparse masked pseudo BCE, normalized ONLY across selected cells
#   - total loss:
#
#         L = L_gold + 0.25 * L_pseudo
#
# IMPORTANT LEAKAGE RULE
# ----------------------
# Outer fold k can ONLY read:
#
#   /kaggle/working/rsna_w2_3/folds/fold_k/
#
# It never uses:
#   - all-58 W2 calibrators
#   - other folds' W2.3 probabilities
#   - cross-fold stability scores
#   - held-out image-fold gold labels for pseudo selection
#
# CONTUSION
# ---------
# No global special case is hardcoded.
# W2.3 availability decides per fold:
#   fold 1: on
#   fold 2: off
#   fold 3: on
#   fold 4: off
#   fold 5: on
#
# if the supplied W2.3 outputs are the validated run.
#
# FAST EXECUTION
# --------------
# No DICOM decoding.
# No ResNet18 image forward pass.
# Only the ~392 MB W3.0 cached [series,16,512] features are loaded.
#
# Expected Kaggle command:
#   !python rsna_w3_1_fold_safe_conservative_weak_supervision.py
# ============================================================

